  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α η : ℝ} (hα : 0 < α) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, α*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v)\n    (hη : 0 < η) {f : E → ℝ} (hf : ContDiff ℝ 1 f) (hc : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let R := fun y : E => μ.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y‖^2/(2*η))\n    let S := fun y : E => (volume : Measure E).tilted\n      (fun u => -V ((1/2:ℝ) • (y+u)) - ‖y-u‖^2/(8*η))\n    (∀ y, S y = (R y).map (fun x : E => (2:ℝ) • x-y)) ∧\n      ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun y : E => ∫ u, f u ∂S y)",
    "statement_sha256": "2ffa67092cac8a25fb4c9aef6cb402b54329b2f9e3d305161a46a6f3e599a6dc",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with canonical Lebesgue/Haar volume and Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. V is globally C2, alpha>0 is a genuine lower Hessian bound and eta>0. The observer f is globally C1 with compact support and can have either sign.",
      "fderiv real (fderiv real V) x v applied to v is the actual directional bilinear Hessian under global C2; its lower bound alpha*norm(v)^2 is explicit. No upper Hessian or upper step restriction appears in this exact analytic statement.",
      "Measure.tilted means actual normalized exponential tilt: mu.tilted(q) has density exp(q)/integral exp(q) dmu when its exponential weight is integrable. Canonical volume is the literal reference measure, never an arbitrary caller density. Probability, partition positivity/finiteness and L1 are not supplied premises.",
      "mu is literally volume.tilted(-V). R(y) is literally its quadratic likelihood tilt -norm(x-y)^2/(2eta). S(y) is literally the displayed volume tilt -V(half*(y+u))-norm(y-u)^2/(8eta), specified at every parameter y. No arbitrary AE conditional version is selected.",
      "Measure.map is the actual measurable pushforward. The map x->2x-y has inverse u->half*(u+y); scale and translation are actual vector operations, not transport certificates. The integral is real Bochner expectation of the arbitrary observer under the exact displayed measure.",
      "ContDiff real1 means global C1 of the exact whole mean function, with genuine continuous Frechet derivative. HasCompactSupport refers to compact closure of its nonzero support. The statement includes no caller law-equality, derivative-continuity, integrability, normalizer or closed-gradient certificate.",
      "No transition trajectory, rough-observer domain, convergence/mixing, numerical error, oracle cost or algorithm complexity claim is supplied by these predicates."
    ]
